# Git never converts line ends here, on any platform: every file is checked out as the bytes that were committed.
# Git for Windows turns core.autocrlf on by default, and a CRLF checkout would change the bytes a plugin's tree hash
# is computed over (verify would call every plugin tampered), the harness template the tests compare with, and the
# shell scripts the hooks run; -text keeps autocrlf away from them. It also keeps a file committed with CRLF (a skill
# `import` copied byte for byte, a log from a Windows machine) as it is: text=auto would store it as LF while the
# working copy kept CRLF, and `release create` then refused a change there was no way to commit (2026-09-23 review).
* -text
